# Lesson 02 – Data Models & TypeScript Interfaces

## Goal

Learn how React + TypeScript organizes data before building components.

---

## What I learned

### 1. Interface vs Class

Unlike Java, React applications usually use **interfaces** instead of classes for data models.

* Java class = blueprint + object creation
* TypeScript interface = blueprint only

The interface does **not** store data.

It only defines how data should look.

---

### 2. Objects store the data

The actual information is stored inside objects.

Example:

```text
Goal Interface
        ↓
Goal Object
        ↓
GoalCard Component
        ↓
Dashboard
```

---

### 3. Separation of Concerns

Each file has one responsibility.

```text
Goal.ts
    Defines what a Goal is.

GoalCard.tsx
    Displays one Goal.

Dashboard.tsx
    Displays many GoalCards.

App.tsx
    Starts the application.
```

---

